1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 d5 4. Bf4 c6 5. e3 Bg7 6. Nf3 O-O 7. Qb3 Qa5 ({I
prefer this to the alternative} 7... dxc4 8. Bxc4 Nbd7 9. Ng5 $1 Qe8 10. Bc7 $1
) 8. Ne5 b6 ({Better, and adequate for equality is} 8... Nh5 {e.g.} 9. cxd5
Nxf4 10. exf4 cxd5 11. Qxd5 Qb6 {regaining the pawn - Gligoric-Boleslavsky,
Saltsjobaden 1948}) 9. Be2 Ba6 10. O-O Rc8 11. Rac1 Nbd7 12. Rfd1 Nxe5 13. Bxe5
dxc4 14. Bxc4 Bxc4 15. Qxc4 b5 16. Qb3 a6 17. Bxf6 Bxf6 18. Ne4 Bg7 19. Rc5 Bf8
20. Rdc1 e6 21. R5c2 Be7 22. h3 Qb6 23. Nc5 a5 24. a4 Rab8 $4 ({An oversight
which loses at once, but Black had a very difficult game anyway:} 24... Bxc5
25. Rxc5 -- 26. Qc2 -- 27. e4 -- 28. d5) (24... b4 25. Nxe6 $1 fxe6 26. Qxe6+
Kf8 27. d5 $1 $18) 25. Nd7 Qd8 26. Nxb8 Rxb8 27. Rxc6 bxa4 28. Qxb8 Qxb8 29.
Rc8+ Qxc8 30. Rxc8+ Kg7 31. Ra8 Bb4 32. Ra7 g5 33. e4 Kg6 34. g4 f6 35. Kf1 h5
36. Ke2 hxg4 37. hxg4 {Source: Universities Chess Annual (2nd issue), Nov 1951}
1-0

