1. d4 e6 2. c4 f5 3. g3 Nf6 4. Bg2 Be7 5. Nf3 O-O 6. O-O d6 7. Nc3 c6 ({The
usual and better move is} 7... Qe8 {Black must try for an early e5.}) 8. Qc2
Nbd7 9. e4 fxe4 10. Nxe4 Nb6 ({Not} 10... e5 11. Neg5 {winning at least a pawn}
) 11. Nxf6+ Bxf6 12. Re1 Qc7 13. c5 {To stop c6-c5 but giving Black the square
d5 for his knight.} Nd5 14. cxd6 Qxd6 15. Ne5 Bxe5 16. dxe5 Qe7 17. Be4 h6 18.
Qe2 Qf7 19. h4 ({The first error.} 19. f4 {is much better}) 19... b6 20. Bd2
Ba6 21. Bg6 Qxg6 22. Qxa6 Rf3 23. Qc4 Raf8 {Threatening Rxg3+} 24. Re2 c5 25.
Kg2 Rd3 {Threatening Rxf2+} 26. Rf1 Rff3 27. Qe4 Qh5 28. Bc1 ({With 13 moves
to make in 4 minutes, White misses} 28. Rfe1 $1 {followed by Be3. Black would
have to play Qf5, which gives him the better ending.}) 28... b5 29. Kh2 Rd4 30.
Qc2 Rxh4+ 31. Kg1 Rh1+ 32. Kg2 Rh2+ 33. Kg1 Qh3 {source: Universities Chess
Annual, 2nd issue, Nov. 1951} 0-1

